Recommended Professions

Lawyer / Legal Counsel

Where it is applied: Law firms, corporate legal departments, government agencies, international organizations (e.g., UN, EU), NGOs focusing on human rights or social justice.

Average salary range in Europe: Highly variable by country and specialization. Entry-level might start around €35,000-€50,000/year, mid-career €60,000-€100,000+, senior/partner level €120,000-€250,000+. (Note: Figures are broad estimates). Median could be around €75,000.

Useful skills: Analytical thinking, critical reasoning, strong research and writing skills, attention to detail, argumentation and persuasion, public speaking, negotiation, ethical judgment, discipline, ability to handle pressure.

Policy Advisor / Analyst

Where it is applied: Government ministries or agencies (national or EU level), political parties, think tanks, non-governmental organizations (NGOs), international organizations, consulting firms specializing in public policy.

Average salary range in Europe: Entry-level €30,000-€45,000/year, mid-career €50,000-€80,000+, senior €80,000-€120,000+. Median around €60,000.

Useful skills: Research and analytical skills, understanding of political and legal systems, data analysis (quantitative and qualitative), strong writing and communication skills (briefings, reports), ability to synthesize complex information, networking, sometimes statistical software proficiency.

Project Manager (especially in Social/Legal/International sectors)

Where it is applied: NGOs, international development agencies, government bodies implementing social programs, tech companies (legal tech), consulting firms managing client projects, large corporations with CSR initiatives.

Average salary range in Europe: Entry-level/Junior PM €35,000-€50,000/year, mid-level PM €55,000-€85,000+, senior/Program Manager €80,000-€130,000+. Median around €70,000.

Useful skills: Leadership, team management, organization and planning, communication (written and verbal), problem-solving, budget management, time management, risk assessment, adaptability, stakeholder management, potentially specific methodologies (Agile, Scrum).

Advice on Next Steps

Research specific program requirements and scholarship opportunities. Focus on the English-taught programs at your preferred universities (like Bologna, Leiden, Trinity). Check their websites for admission criteria (grades, required subjects, English proficiency test scores like IELTS or TOEFL) and application deadlines. Crucially, investigate scholarships available specifically for Ukrainian citizens, both from the universities themselves and national governments (e.g., Italian government scholarships like MAECI). Starting early is key.